# Documentation stays current

User-facing behavior changes are unfinished until **`docs/content/`** matches. Update those pages in the same session as the code. When committing, keep a separate `docs:` commit (see the commits rule).

`README.md` is marketing for GitHub. It links to [devenv4monorepo.github.io](https://devenv4monorepo.github.io/) and the [contribution guide](https://devenv4monorepo.github.io/#contributing). Do **not** copy option tables, command matrices, or layout dumps into the README. A one-line pitch change does not require a docs edit.

## Where the docs live

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| Flake pin, consumer layout, `devenv.local.nix` | `docs/content/apply.md` |
| `setup.sh`, `home-switch`, everyday commands | `docs/content/bootstrap.md` |
| `languages.*`, `supported.*`, catalog, Rust edition | `docs/content/languages.md` |
| Git hooks, commitlint, tag guard (user-facing) | `docs/content/hooks.md` |
| Terminal, Quake, Cursor, Home Manager | `docs/content/terminal.md` |
| Workflows, BATS, JUnit, Pages URL | `docs/content/ci.md` |
| Package / consumer layout reference | `docs/content/reference.md` |
| Architecture / motivation | `docs/content/architecture.md`, `overview.md` |
| New or retired shipped tool | `docs/content/tools.md` (docs + donate link if the project publishes one) |
| Package development, tests, catalog, layout, Pages | `docs/content/contributing.md` |
| New top-level topic | new `docs/content/<id>.md`, import `?raw` in `docs/src/sections.ts` |

## Do

- Name the real option, script, workflow, or file.
- Add or drop sidenav headings by editing `##` lines; `sections.ts` derives ids from those titles.
- Document package-first consumption (flake pin), not Copier template copy.
- Link the live site as `https://devenv4monorepo.github.io/` (section hashes like `#contributing`).

```
# ❌ BAD — rustc floor changed, languages.md still says 1.80
# ✅ GOOD — languages.md says 2024 needs rustc 1.85; README stays a pitch
```

## Do not

- Mirror docs tables into `README.md`.
- Leave Copier questionnaire / answers-file language in user-facing docs.
- Invent flags or paths that are not in the tree.
